- Story & Context: At the Oasis of Low-Bit, the keeper known as Jora demands a precise voltage-controlled input before she grants access to the coolant supply. The exchange is tense because the nomad-trader only has a corrupted cassette of a synth-solo to offer as payment. "Turn the dial until the desert stops screaming."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Close up of two hands touching a corroded copper dial, desert heat waves blurring the background, hyper-realistic, grit and rust texture.

Track 3: The Transit of Venusian Ghosts
- Story & Context: After the great caravan fire, the elders claim the spirit of the lost Prophet-5 resides in the planetarium ruins, haunting the frequency spectrum. Travelers report that if you play the forbidden scale during the transit, the walls begin to glow with the ghosts of forgotten data. "The stars are just holes where the light escaped our grasp."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A desolate, domed ruins lit by a strange, pulsating violet light, star field visible through the crumbling ceiling, surreal, haunting.

